    "abstract": "A study of the decays $B_{s}^{0} \\\\to \\\\mu^{+}\\\\mu^{-}$ and $B^{0} \\\\to \\\\mu^{+}\\\\mu^{-}$ has been performed using 26.3 fb$^{-1}$ of 13 TeV LHC proton-proton collision data collected with the ATLAS detector in 2015 and 2016. The measured branching fraction for $B_{s}^{0} \\\\to \\\\mu^{+}\\\\mu^{-}$ is $\\\\mathcal{B}(B_{s}^{0}\\\\to\\\\mu^{+}\\\\mu^{-}) = (3.2 \\\\pm 0.9) \\\\times 10^{-9}$ and an upper limit of $\\\\mathcal{B}(B^{0}\\\\to\\\\mu^{+}\\\\mu^{-}) < 4.3 \\\\times 10^{-10}$ at 95% CL is set. A combination with the ATLAS Run 1 results is also performed.",
